# calls-arith.c compiled with -g gives the same transcript as without -g, at
# -O0 and at -O2 (Milestone 4, review-r2 findings 1 and 3; Milestone 7,
# review-r1 finding 3). The -O2 leg covers the two Milestone-4 failures, which
# need -O1 or above: with -g at -O1 and above clang turns on call-site info
# (EmitCallSiteInfo), which the MSIL call lowering must keep in step when it
# splits and recombines a call ('Call site info was not updated!'), and every
# x86_64 triple defaults to instruction-referencing variable locations, whose
# LiveDebugValues assumes the allocated physical registers that MSIL never has
# (main's named integer locals, such as one, seven and big, carry #dbg_value
# records). The -O0 leg is the mode in which every parameter and local is a
# #dbg_declare of a frame slot, which static frames (M7) make reachable. The
# expected transcript is calls-arith.expected, which update-expected.py
# generates for calls-arith.c; calls-arith.c runs the same pipeline without -g
# at every level of %{msil_c}, and each leg here is one level of it plus -g.
# The RUN lines are Phase 1's pipeline (clang -S, ilasm -dll), which the lit
# parameter msil_pipeline does not switch, so the test runs only under the
# default pipeline asm (plan 5.12.13; the lto and obj legs would repeat it
# unchanged).
# REQUIRES: msil-pipeline=asm

# RUN: %clang_msil %{msil_cflags} -O0 -g -S %S/calls-arith.c -o %t.O0.il
# RUN: %ilasm -dll -output=%t.O0.dll %t.O0.il
# RUN: %msil_verify %t.O0.dll
# RUN: %if msil-jitall %{ %msil_jitall %t.O0.dll %}
# RUN: %msil_exec --expect %S/calls-arith --out %t.O0.out %t.O0.dll

# RUN: %clang_msil %{msil_cflags} -O2 -g -S %S/calls-arith.c -o %t.O2.il
# RUN: %ilasm -dll -output=%t.O2.dll %t.O2.il
# RUN: %msil_verify %t.O2.dll
# RUN: %if msil-jitall %{ %msil_jitall %t.O2.dll %}
# RUN: %msil_exec --expect %S/calls-arith --out %t.O2.out %t.O2.dll
